e database service rather than on disk, and the\nbackend proxies them out at /api/images/{id}/content. The browser only\never holds an image ID, so nothing about the storage layout leaks into\nthe frontend.\n\nImageRules holds the limits away from the request pipeline so they can\nbe tested directly: a size ceiling, a per-post count, an allowed content\ntype list, and a check that the bytes really are the format they claim\nrather than trusting the declared type. Uploading and deleting are\nrestricted to the author of the post or comment; reading is open to\neveryone, as the rest of the forum is.\n\n* refactor: tighten AI mode error handling and stale comments\n\nMatch the assistant error on the ApiError type rather than on its name\nstring. The old check turned on a name that nothing enforces, and it had\nto be read alongside the stream reader to see why a plain Error was\nallowed past it; the reason is now written down next to the check.\n\nCorrect two comments in the assistant wiring that no longer described\nthe code: one named a model size the service does not use, and the\nOllama address had picked up a second comment saying what the first\nalready said.\n\n* feat(forum): source forums from the course catalogue\n\nReplace the hardcoded forum list with a Forums table synced from the quizzes\nand courses catalogue, and move Posts from a Category string to a ForumId FK.\n\nForums are matched by course ID, so renaming a course renames its forum and\nkeeps the posts in it. A forum''s code is written once and never resynced,\nbecause URLs are /forums/:code and existing links must keep working. Nothing\nis ever deleted, since a withdrawn course would orphan its posts. The sync\nruns once at start-up and an unreachable catalogue is not fatal.\n\nA volume created before forums existed is migrated on start-up: each distinct\nPosts.Category becomes a forum and its posts are repointed at it.\n\nAn unknown forum in a GET /api/posts filter is no longer a validation error.\nIt simply matches nothing, which removes a round trip from every read.\n\n* test(forum): cover the course sync and category migration\n\nAdd a Db.Tests project, modelled on the sibling quizzes-courses one: a\nthrowaway SQLite file per test, initialised from the real schema.sql and\nseed.sql rather than a copy of them.\n\nForumSyncTests covers matching by course ID, adopting a forum that has no\ncourse yet, keeping the forum code when a course changes its own, adding a\nforum for an unmatched course, never deleting, and idempotency.\n\nCategoryMigrationTests builds a genuine pre-forums volume and asserts the\nmigration mints one forum per category, repoints the posts, keeps the\ncomments hanging off them, and does not seed over what it just migrated.\n\n* docs: describe how discussion forums track the course catalogue\n\nDocument the sync in the root readme: course-ID matching, write-once forum\ncodes, why nothing is deleted, the non-fatal failure path, and the migration\nthat carries a pre-forums volume across.\n\n* feat: add login support for quizzes and courses\n\n* feat: make login page look pretty + enhance safe return logic\n\n* feat: add flashcards, quizzes, milestones + lesson completion + split seeding into separate sql fies\n\n* Game Database Setup and docker config\n\n* feat: Garry.\n\n* Frontend overhaul\n\n* Test fixes\n\n* Add word sourcing from language course content\n\n* Add AI Generated Word Lists To Mini games\n\n* feat: add template db project\n\n* feat: add skeleton backend project\n\n* feat: add skeleton frontend project\n\n* chore: register with compose and shared frontend\n\n* fix: build errors\n\n* chore: remove vuetify dependency\n\n* feat: add leaderboard to page\n\n* feat: add ci\n\n* chore: change conflicting port\n\n* feat: implement sidebar\n\n* feat: add auth\n\n* feat: add mock lessons completed chart\n\n* feat: only show analytics to logged in users\n\n* feat: only show rankings for current user\n\n* feat: add ai summary card\n\n* reset default\n\n* chore: align styles 1\n\n* feat: add gary to chatdiscussion\n\n* chore: align styles 2\n\n* reset default\n\n* fix merge error\n\n* feat: chatdiscussion garry error message\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Lachlan Giang <lachlan.giang@wisetechglobal.com>\nCo-authored-by: Justin Wong <justinwong124@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kyan Grimm <Kyan.J.Grimm@student.uts.edu.au>\nCo-authored-by: Roan.VanElven <Roan.VanElven@wisetechglobal.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmLEwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzukQAGP0wcV0N+ZXRBqSVHCFIDsY\n+S+E1Q8mkRktanMY5ZTA4nJWxDrGNOTHkzlUjr7y7w9Qx0jewTZSmk3hA3QOQZNa\nvifl9qxQnUru45dbaWNMIvhZ6RCdTCf1HmkoaRTA6n+vhKFVEozyogvSyWLVvy1i\nbnbiX5DLRoQ3Y9ECoMz+y9/SCQQeKqOEIlwO3qQhqTaPJfINxX9fXl2XHey3OJP5\noR/HhHVfFwW5ayNwntQigtyywTkKd3MyxnQRVepMEaMN/ZFdiR6dcIXf6WCNtQgA\nTx14XD49KJupbW1D3jnOV9kRMKnlFOmrLaujVuo2+s3wof6aGkFbrDgNKJIw+v4m\nLu3ygggR4a3vtBzy7YM0IM8AD6RRESnkZO4WoLESvIv7Do5j3TE+9A1Gp6dUKJCT\nXLImCBKnmrhjfEIBMLXBWrIVYXTCv8kFs/RonAQuo+RxovtUMdrnHCU8G8+yHlff\nGjEl7Tak1VSBUnzF/mR6LvfYLCtTTFKCHdBb8zYj7b/Esct8W4KfXL4RWjFehVIn\nUqcmWOu7QO6fKzrB80QKNT9CQKcuKbZh+6jtPCcgQnmbkt4XehJooHuGgUQ4oLQ4\ny2G4XMUkfh7IZHJHWIG5u3xDvGS9RxSXp69wz3CooUhtE7jlZq+1c0d/IvFaWuHm\ne1MRaJPq+1z7cKQ6IXwq\n=NbPi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T23:28:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url