red{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZrisanDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZrisanDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZrisanDev/front-hce/commits/fe90ab47e31197fc5ca6629c8e52435b2ef3fca7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:33:08Z","email":"gabriel.andrade.0296@gmail.com","name":"ZrisanDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:33:08Z","email":"gabriel.andrade.0296@gmail.com","name":"ZrisanDev"},"message":"feat(shared/auth): add AuthProvider, useAuth hook, and AuthGuard\n\n- use-auth.ts: AuthContext + useAuth() (throws when used outside AuthProvider).\n- auth-provider.tsx: optimistic AuthProvider. The HttpOnly cookie can''t be read\n  and there is no /auth/me, so it starts ''checking'' and optimistically becomes\n  ''authenticated'' on mount; any 401 (via subscribeSessionExpired) flips it to\n  ''guest''. login() calls apiClient.auth.login (throws ApiError -> form shows it)\n  then resetSessionExpired() + ''authenticated''. logout() -> ''guest''.\n- guard.tsx: guest -> hard redirect to ROUTES.login (window.location, cross-zone)\n  in an effect; checking -> skeleton; authenticated -> children.\n\nState is intentionally NOT synced across zones (each zone is a separate app).\nExported from @hce/shared/auth and the root @hce/shared barrel.\n\nVerification: bunx tsc --noEmit -p packages/shared/tsconfig.json -> exit 0.","tree":{"sha":"551eead21fa9736e57d6794a213ee5fced778eb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZrisanDev/front-hce/git/trees/551eead21fa9736e57d6794a213ee5fced778eb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZrisanDev/front-hce/git/commits/fe90ab47e31197fc5ca6629c8e52435b2ef3fca7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103600178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZrisanDev/events