rshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/commits/e7f7a6edf46c84e71e246aa03dd45e90b86fafbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:26:13Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:26:13Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: keep settings in step across JupyterLab windows\n\nEach JupyterLab window keeps its own copy of the settings and writes\nthe whole copy on every save, so a window opened earlier put old values\nback and Claude''s Skip Permissions kept turning itself off. A change now\nposts on a BroadcastChannel so the browser''s other windows reload, and a\nwindow checks the server''s copy when it gains focus; it reloads only when\nthat copy differs, which leaves an open JSON settings editor alone and\nends the echo between windows. A window on another device that saves\nwithout gaining focus first still needs a version check in JupyterLab\ncore (DEF-PANE-283).\n\nThe Galata stub CLI now runs until the test server stops, because a stub\nthat ended after 120 s changed a later test''s terminal count, and the\nDEF-115 test presses Escape on the menu itself.","tree":{"sha":"5b776eee7a7c862f9e3fa0938aedce72aabd65f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/trees/5b776eee7a7c862f9e3fa0938aedce72aabd65f1"},"url":"h