tps://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/commits/838d8e9fdc2e158824dc2d5c5e418b46c70470a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:50:31Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:50:31Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: rename a conversation in the assistant''s own store, and cover every acceptance criterion\n\nRename Session writes a conversation''s name where the assistant itself reads\nit back, because a name kept only in this extension would disagree with the\nCLI the moment either side wrote one. Each store does it its own way - Claude\nappends the record its own /rename writes, Kimi sets a custom title in its\nsession state, Gemini stamps the summary on every metadata record, DeepSeek\nrewrites the newest title event. Codex declares can_rename False: its names\nlive in a sqlite index this store opens read-only and the CLI has no rename\nverb, so the menu item is absent rather than offering an action that fails.\n\nEvery store restores the conversation''s mtime after writing. Without it a\nrename counted as a turn: Claude''s thirty-day switch stamp, which decides what\n`claude -c` resumes, was spent by the write, and a week-idle Kimi, Gemini or\nDeepSeek row jumped to the top of Recent carrying a time the assistant never\nspoke. Restoring the mtime forces FileMemo.drop, since the memo keys on\n(mtime, size) and a name of equal length leaves both halves identical.\n\nTest coverage now reaches all 181 acceptance criteria, with no NO-TEST column\nleft in any of the fourteen categories, and every test was shown able to fail\nby severing the behaviour it guards. Three guard modules cover what had none:\nthe Python core is scanned for assistant names as the TypeScript core already\nwas, the shipped settings schema is held against the provider registry, and\nthe Galata harness''s own configuration is asserted rather than assumed - a rig\nthat is wrong does not fail, it passes against the wrong thing.\n\nDEF-PROV-259 fixed, DEF-FRONT-260 and DEF-PANE-261 wontfix, DEF-GUARD-262\nfixed: the route-gating test claimed every provider route while checking seven\nof the ten registered.","tree":{"sha":"5b6362ee5c2bbb4c0697eb2eb1526722c9bf6f7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/trees/5b6362ee5c2bbb4c0697eb2eb1526722c9bf6f7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/commits/838d8e9fdc2e158824dc2d5c5e418b46c70470a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"htt