en@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: one approval switch per provider, neutral header launch button\n\nDEF-111: Gemini''s settings collapse to the single yoloMode switch like\nevery other provider - the four-rung approvalMode enum is deleted from\nthe descriptor, the schema, the server''s argv mapping and the resolver.\nWith no enum consumer left, the enum machinery goes with it: ILaunchMode\nloses kind/values/unsafeValues, resolveLaunchMode is force-wins-else-\nfirst-true-boolean, the schema generator and the descriptor-parity\nflattening simplify. auto_edit and plan are no longer settable; a stale\napprovalMode key or token is ignored on both runtimes, test-pinned.\n\nDEF-112: the header new-session button paints + unconditionally - the\n_repaintNewIcon hook and the DEF-35 glyph-follows-mode rule are deleted.\nThe armed mode is still named in the button''s tooltip (DEF-36); the\nshield keeps its menu-entry home, with its Galata rendered proof moved\nto Resume (Skip Permissions) identified by path data.\n\nJest 118, pytest 170, Galata 28/28 at v1.0.22, rendered proof\nscreenshotted. Ledger DEF-111/DEF-112, eight acc-crit criteria closed,\njournal entries 29-30, changelog 1.0.23, README launch-modes line.","tree":{"sha":"2bc432a45d0dd59a7fb468091b18e876329294c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/trees/2bc432a45d0dd59a7fb468091b18e876329294c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/commits/8c64fe47cc5fce42dabf3be9a1538e96bbcac27b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/ot