mit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:08:30Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:08:30Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: switch-path contract truth and close-19 defect campaign\n\n- close all 19 open ledger defects via five file-partitioned fix lanes:\n  error-copy pass, fork colour-queue drain, single recentLimit home\n  (src/core/limits.ts), namingStrategy collapse, state-write logging,\n  metadata cache caps, settings read-once, IOLoop discipline, migration\n  end-to-end test, guard line-skew fix, timeout parity test, and the\n  background-agent chip Galata proof\n- fix the four campaign-seeded regressions the re-confirm rounds caught:\n  loop-owned state writes reverted off the executor (DEF-99), DEF-76\n  hunks re-landed after a cross-lane restore clobber (DEF-100), claude''s\n  store-internal pin write deleted (DEF-101), and the switch response\n  re-resolved after the route-side pin so a pinned project''s switch no\n  longer toasts a spurious failure (DEF-102)\n- slim the store switch contract to {\"requested\"}: the route owns the\n  pin and the post-pin current; four store-side resolutions deleted and\n  every switch docstring made truthful (DEF-103, DEF-105, DEF-106,\n  DEF-109)\n- grow the ledger to 110 entries, 0 open, recording per-provider probe\n  matrices, two reviewer-claim retractions, and four logged-not-fixed\n  rulings (DEF-104, DEF-107, DEF-108, DEF-110)\n- adversarial rounds 8-20, round 20 clean on both lenses; pytest 170,\n  Jest 121, Galata 27/27, prettier clean","tree":{"sha":"1211fa50896a0ca685bcec148b268f85e13b1d4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/trees/1211fa50896a0ca685bcec148b268f85e13b1d4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/commits/7766d140e243b6813ec484e8b5e315d5f4cd2a1d","verification":{"payloa