eb85ce755db16d8b7928280daccee9b3c679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/commits/212aeb85ce755db16d8b7928280daccee9b3c679"}],"sha":"005fdc0dd10253807f7167ff93da852b13496e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/commits/005fdc0dd10253807f7167ff93da852b13496e71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/commits/212aeb85ce755db16d8b7928280daccee9b3c679/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:50:23Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:50:23Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: close the adversarial campaign at v1.0.8 - 74 defects fixed, 8 logged\n\nSix adversarial review rounds over the consolidated extension, with every\nfinding triaged against the code before acting. 82 defects recorded: 74\nclosed, 8 left open with the reason each was left.\n\nFrontend:\n- bound every server call at 60s (DEF-72), above codex.py''s own 30s CLI\n  timeout so a fork is not cut on the slow path it was tuned for\n- serialise ColourStore behind a single promise chain (DEF-30), deleting\n  the write/read sequence machinery four earlier rewrites had accumulated\n- settle the colour queue before a fork snapshots its parent (DEF-31)\n- route refused branches through _showActionError, so codex, gemini and\n  kimi stop promising a retry that never happens (the half of DEF-53 its\n  own note was silent about)\n- name the settings defaults and clamp bounds once (DEF-71)\n\nServer:\n- read the configured user-settings dir rather than JupyterLab''s default,\n  in both the provider gate and the migration path (DEF-63)\n- hash UTF-8 bytes on both sides of the wire, so a conversation tints the\n  same colour whichever runtime resolved it (DEF-52)\n\nGuards and tests:\n- derive the core-neutrality name list from the registry (DEF-58)\n- compare launch-mode enum VALUES across runtimes, not just ids (DEF-59)\n- fail the parity suite against a stale lib/ instead of certifying it\n  silently (DEF-60)\n- new panel suite and a Galata tier giving six panel defects rendered\n  proof in a real browser rather than a jsdom argument (DEF-62)\n\nThe last wave is deliberately two lines. 11 of the 75 defects were created\nby a previous fix and six of the nine causing fixes were MINORs, so round\n6''s remaining findings are logged as DEF-76..DEF-82 rather than fixed -\neach entry carrying the mechanism, corrected against its reviewer, and the\nreason it was left.\n\npytest 163, Jest 119, Galata 26/26, tsc clean, eslint 0 errors.","tree":{"sha":"aebe4da38c6ccc3781e2fe89065cc03658a58d52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_code_assistants_extension/git/trees/aebe4da38c6ccc3781e2fe89065cc03658a58d52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_ai_c