d6115a9ed8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T04:33:46Z","email":"124170011+TusharEmran@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharEmran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T04:33:46Z","email":"124170011+TusharEmran@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharEmran"},"message":"Scaffold CinemaSeat project structure, infra, and design docs\n\nLays out the skeleton for a cinema seat-booking system whose central\nconstraint is that a seat is never sold twice. This commit is mostly\nstructure and stated intent rather than behavior.\n\nImplemented:\n- db/schema.ts: Drizzle schema for movies, theatres, showtimes, seats\n  and prices, plus the seat_claims table whose unique index is what\n  makes double-booking impossible\n- config/env.ts: startup env parsing, including HOLD_TTL_SECONDS\n- docker compose stack (nginx, api, worker, postgres, redis, mock\n  gateway), Dockerfiles, CI/CD workflows, Makefile\n- README, architecture/API/runbook docs, decision log, mermaid\n  diagrams, k6 load scenarios, shell drills\n\nScaffolded only, each carrying a header comment that specifies the\ncontract it must satisfy followed by a TODO:\n- seating (hold claim/release, seatmap, cache), booking state machine,\n  payment (gateway client, callbacks, OTP, signatures), catalog\n- app/main/worker wiring, db client/migrate/seed/bootstrap, logging,\n  error handling, rate limiting, circuit breaker\n- every frontend page and component\n- unit and integration test bodies\n\nAlso fixes backend/tsconfig.json, where rootDir src contradicted the\ntests/** include: emit settings moved to tsconfig.build.json and the\ndeprecated baseUrl was dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dfc6efcf4eeb38e280d3454cf7ac9aa8348c480","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/git/trees/9dfc6efcf4eeb38e280d3454cf7ac9aa8348c480"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/git/commits/b747238ecb58750bd196cbd57021cdd6115a9ed8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124170011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharEmran","id":124170011,"login":"TusharEmran","node_id":"U_kgDOB2avGw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/commit/b747238ecb58750bd196cbd57021cdd6115a9ed8","node_id":"C_kwDOTx6qPdoAKGI3NDcyMzhlY2I1ODc1MGJkMTk2Y2JkNTcwMjFjZGQ2MTE1YTllZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/commit/75102479c0782945598307dcf857b51a77601869","sha":"75102479c0782945598307dcf857b51a77601869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/commits/75102479c0782945598307dcf857b51a77601869"}],"sha":"b747238ecb58750bd196cbd57021cdd6115a9ed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TusharEmran/CinemaSeat/commits/b747238ecb58750bd196cbd57021cdd6115a9ed8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124170011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharEmran/foll